{
  "status": "ok",
  "data": {
    "query": "Xi Jinping Boao Forum trade opening April 2018 China US talks",
    "search_window": {
      "from": "2018-01-11",
      "to": "2018-04-11"
    },
    "sources": {
      "grounding": {
        "generic": [
          {
            "url": "https://www.bloomberg.com/news/live-blog/2018-04-06/chinese-president-xi-jinping-speaks-at-boao-forum",
            "title": "Chinese President Xi Jinping Speaks at Boao Forum - Bloomberg Business",
            "snippets": [
              "# Chinese President Xi Jinping Speaks at Boao Forum\nWelcome to TOPLive! Join us on Tuesday, April 10, for Chinese President Xi Jinping (pictured)'s keynote address at the Boao Forum for Asia Annual Conference 2018 in southern China's Hainan province.",
              "Today's speech is something of a balancing act for Xi. On one hand it's an opportunity to tell an audience of global investors and executives that China is open for business and welcomes foreign competition",
              "On the other hand, though, Xi will need to strike back at Donald trump's aggressive trade rhetoric by promising to defend his nation's interests. Either way, Xi's message will set the tone for the next phase of the trade tensions.",
              "There's an air of expectation among China watchers that Xi will detail parts of the economy where greater foreign competition will be welcomed. But the devil will be in the detail.\n\nChinese officials have often promised greater access to sectors such as banking or to buy more U.S. beef, only for progress to be painstakingly slow. It's the reason foreign executives complain of 'promise fatigue.'",
              "In case you missed it, here's a preview we wrote of today's speech. Fraser Howie, co-author of the book “Red Capitalism” summed it up best when he said Xi has to both preach openness but also push back.\n\nXi Takes Center Stage to Defend China's Trade From Trump Barrage\n\nShare on Twitter Share on Facebook 2018-04-10T01:21:26.062+00:00\n\nKen Wills Beijing Bureau Chief",
              "President Xi's speech could offer a face-saving resolution to U.S.-China trade tensions. As his top economic adviser Liu He said at Davos: China is ready to surprise the world with reforms. If Xi does just that, Trump can claim victory and say it was all because of his tariff threats. China can say it was unrelated and was telegraphed long before. Both sides can step away from the brink of a trade war and play to their domestic audiences",
              "Trump Hints at Deal on Chinese Trade as Xi Readies Response\n\nShare on Twitter Share on Facebook 2018-04-10T01:26:57.399+00:00\n\nQi Ding China Breaking News Team\n\nThe opening ceremony of Boao Forum is scheduled at 9:30am. Xi will speak after former Japanese PM Yasuo Fukuda's welcome address, according to the official schedule",
              "Share on Twitter Share on Facebook 2018-04-10T01:28:32.314+00:00\n\nEmma O'Brien Global Markets Editor ek_obrien\n\nGiven the broad, almost vague approach Xi takes to these kind of speeches, I'm not expecting any immediate market reaction -- unless he goes off piste and announces the next set of retaliatory measures in the trade fight with Trump",
              "Here's an indication of the 'promise fatigue' that Western executives are experiencing when it comes to China. Myron Brilliant, head of international affairs at the U.S. Chamber of Commerce, told Bloomberg TV earlier that Xi's speech will need to go well beyond rhetoric and offer specific details on where he plans to allow more foreign competition.\n\n\"We’re looking for action after this speech.\"",
              "President Xi Jinping starts keynote speech at Boao Forum.",
              "If Xi pushes hard on the trade button in this speech today, we may see reaction in mainland Chinese and Hong Kong stocks - mostly because people aren't expecting him to be pointed on that front.\n\nChinese stocks barely reacted, for example, when the U.S. released its list of 1,333 imports from China that it would target with tariffs, but those in Hong Kong sold off quite strongly later that day, when China unexpectedly matched Trump's 25 percent tariff on things like airplanes and soybeans",
              "President Xi Jinping starts keynote speech at Boao Forum.\nXi Talks About Globalization in Beginning of Speech Xi Talks About Globalization in Beginning of Speech",
              "China's Xi Says Should Push for Free Trade\nChina Stocks Diverge: Shanghai Composite Up, Small Caps Down China Stocks Diverge: Shanghai Composite Up, Small Caps Down\nShare on Twitter Share on Facebook 2018-04-10T02:03:36.483+00:00\nEmma O'Brien Global Markets Editor ek_obrien\nSome interesting divergence taking place in China's stock market as this speech powers on",
              "China will explore the opening of free-trade ports with Chinese characteristics -- interesting.",
              "Share on Twitter Share on Facebook 2018-04-10T02:10:50.229+00:00\nEnda Curran Chief Asia Economics Correspondent endacurran\nOn manufacturing, Xi said they have basically opened up, barring cars and ships and aircraft. But he says they will ease foreign equity restrictions in the car industry, especially.\nXi Says China Will Strengthen Property-Rights Protection, Oppose Monopolies Xi Says China Will Strengthen Property-Rights Protection, Oppose Monopolies",
              "That was a specific complaint of Trump's.",
              "Share on Twitter Share on Facebook 2018-04-10T02:15:16.909+00:00\nKen Wills Beijing Bureau Chief\nXi's offering broad promises to ease investment restrictions, especially for the auto sector, as well as opening for more foreign investment in shipping, aviation, financial sectors. IPR protections and tariff relief are also on the menu. This will probably be followed in days ahead by ministries issuing specific details."
            ]
          },
          {
            "url": "https://www.cnbc.com/2018/04/09/chinese-president-xi-jinping-speaks-at-boao-forum-for-asia.html",
            "title": "Chinese President Xi Jinping speaks at Boao Forum for Asia",
            "snippets": [
              "# China's Xi announces plans to 'open' China, including lowering tariffs on imported autos\n- President Xi Jinping announces plans to open up China's economy, including lowering tariffs for autos and enforcing the legal intellectual property of foreign firms.\n- Xi outlines his plans at the Boao Forum for Asia on the same day the World Trade Organization said China filed a complaint challenging President Donald Trump's tariffs on imported steel and aluminum.\n\nPresident Xi Jinping vows 'further opening' of China's economy",
              "President Xi Jinping vows 'further opening' of China's economy\n\nSquawk Box Asia\n\nChinese President Xi Jinping announced plans on Tuesday to open up the Chinese economy, including lowering tariffs for autos and other products and enforcing the legal intellectual property of foreign firms.\n\nXi's comments come amid escalating trade tensions between China and the U.S. as the world's two largest economies take turns announcing punitive trade measures against each other",
              "In a speech at the Boao Forum for Asia, an annual summit that's been dubbed the \"Asian Davos,\" Xi said China will take the initiative to expand imports this year and \"work hard\" to import products that are required by the population.\n\n\"China does not seek [a] trade surplus. We have a genuine desire to increase imports and achieve greater balance of international payments under the current account,\" Xi said, according to a translation of the speech",
              "Beyond that, he described China as a country upon which other nations had imposed unfair trade penalties: \"We hope developed countries will stop imposing restrictions on normal and reasonable trade of high-tech products and relax export controls on such trade with China,\" he said, not naming any specific country.\n\nIn his speech, the Chinese president sold a vision of China as a benevolent leader of the global economy, emphasizing that open systems are the best course of action for the world",
              "Instead, he said, countries should \"stay committed to openness, connectivity and mutual benefits, build an open global economy, and reinforce cooperation within the G-20, APEC and other multilateral frameworks. We should promote trade and investment liberalization and facilitation, support the multilateral trading system.\"\n\n\"This way, we will make economic globalization, more open, inclusive, balanced and beneficial to all,\" he added",
              "One way is by pushing China's state intellectual property office this year to step up law enforcement of relevant laws, Xi said.\n\n\"We encourage normal technological exchanges and cooperation between Chinese and foreign enterprises and protect the lawful [intellectual property] owned by foreign enterprises in China,\" he said.\n\nTrump is taking Beijing to task over China's large trade deficit with the U.S., which Washington says is in part due to unfair trade practices",
              "## 'Belt and Road'\nWhile the project may be initiated by China, the opportunities and outcomes will benefit the world, said Xi.\n\n\"China has no geopolitical calculations, seeks no exclusionary blocs and imposes no business deals on others,\" the Chinese president added.",
              "{\"headline\":\"China's Xi announces plans to 'open' China, including lowering tariffs on imported autos\",\"dateCreated\":\"2018-04-10T02:15:41+0000\",\"datePublished\":\"2018-04-10T02:15:41+0000\",\"dateModified\":\"2018-04-11T02:53:00+0000\",\"author\":[{\"name\":\"Everett Rosenfeld\"},{\"name\":\"Huileng Tan\"}],\"publisher\":{\"name\":\"CNBC\",\"foundingDate\":\"1989-04-17\",\"sameAs\":[\"https://www.facebook.com/cnbc\",\"https://www.instagram.com/cnbc\",\"https://www.linkedin.com/company/cnbc\",\"https://twitter.com/cnbc\",\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/CNBC\",\"https://www.youtube.com/cnbc\"]},\"articleSection\":\"Business News\",\"keywords\":[\"cnbc\",\"Articles\",\"Along the Belt and Road\",\"Washington D.C.\",\"Trade\",\"Donald J. Trump\",\"United States\",\"Xi Jinping\",\"Beijing\",\"Politics\",\"China\",\"Asia News\",\"Markets\",\"Asia Economy\",\"Business News\",\"Economy\",\"World Economy\",\"source:tagname:CNBC Asia Source\"],\"video\":{\"description\":\"Chinese President Xi Jinping said the country will \\\"significantly broaden\\\" market access among other measures.\",\"duration\":\"PT7M52S\",\"name\":\"President Xi Jinping vows 'further opening' of China's economy\",\"uploadDate\":\"2018-04-10T00:46:11+0000\"}}"
            ]
          },
          {
